<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's NLCF says to seek 53,500T of oilseeds.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's NLCF says to seek 53,500T of oilseeds.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's National Livestock Cooperative Federation (NLCF) will invite tenders to buy a total of 53,500 tonnes of oilseeds by 11:00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, an official with the federation said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tenders broke down into 14,000 tonnes of rapeseed meal, 6,500 tonnes of cottonseed meal, 8,000 tonnes of grain screening pellet and 25,000 tonnes of palm kernel meal, the NLCF official said.  </p>
<p>If it passes on the tenders in whole or partially on Tuesday due to high prices, it will re-invite the tenders on April 25.</p>
<p>Details for the tenders are as follows:</p>
<p>    COMMODS		  TONNE   ETA     ARRIVAL PORT</p>
<p>    rapeseed meal	  7,000   Sep 20  Inchon</p>
<p>    rapeseed meal	  7,000   Sep 30  Kunsan/Ulsan</p>
<p>    cottonseed meal	6,500   Oct 10  Inchon</p>
<p>    GSP			4,000   Jul 20  Inchon/Ulsan</p>
<p>    GSP			4,000   Sep 20  Inchon/Ulsan</p>
<p>    palm kernel meal     5,000   Jun 30  Kunsan/Ulsan</p>
<p>    palm kernel meal     5,000   Jun 30  Inchon</p>
<p>    palm kernel meal     5,000   Jul 30  Kunsan/Ulsan</p>
<p>    palm kernel meal     5,000   Aug 10  Inchon</p>
<p>    palm kernel meal     5,000   Sep 10  Kunsan/Ulsan</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
